---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Mar Azul Invests in Public Electrical Infrastructure for Las Flores Road | Coyol Real Estate">
  <article class="blog-post">
    <header class="post-header">
      <p class="category">Infrastructure</p>
      <h1>Mar Azul Developers Building Electrical Main Lines for Las Flores Road</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">Private investment in public infrastructure to benefit the entire Nosara community</p>
      <time datetime="2026-08-01">August 1, 2026</time>
    </header>

    <figure class="hero-image">
      <img src="/images/mar-azul/electric-infrastructure.jpg" alt="Electrical infrastructure installation on Las Flores Road" />
      <figcaption>New electrical main lines being installed along Las Flores Road</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="post-content">
      <p class="lead">The developers of Mar Azul are currently undertaking a significant infrastructure project: building and donating electrical main lines along Las Flores Road. Once completed, this infrastructure will be transferred to ICE (Instituto Costarricense de Electricidad), Costa Rica's national electric utility, to serve the broader community.</p>

      <h2>Beyond Private Development</h2>
      
      <p>While many developments focus solely on their own infrastructure needs, Mar Azul has consistently taken a different approach. The Las Flores Road electrical project extends far beyond the boundaries of the Mar Azul community, bringing reliable power infrastructure to an area that has long needed it.</p>
      
      <p>This isn't the first time Mar Azul's developers have invested in public infrastructure. The same team previously donated a water system to ASADA Santa Marta that now serves over 250 local families.</p>

      <h2>The Project</h2>
      
      <div class="stats-block">
        <div class="stat">
          <span class="number">800m</span>
          <span class="label">Line extension</span>
        </div>
        <div class="stat">
          <span class="number">ICE</span>
          <span class="label">Receiving utility</span>
        </div>
        <div class="stat">
          <span class="number">100%</span>
          <span class="label">Privately funded</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p>The electrical infrastructure project includes:</p>
      
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Main electrical lines</strong> along Las Flores Road</li>
        <li><strong>Transformer installations</strong> to serve multiple properties</li>
        <li><strong>Connection points</strong> for existing and future homes in the area</li>
        <li><strong>Full compliance</strong> with ICE technical standards</li>
      </ul>
      
      <p>Upon completion, the entire system will be donated to ICE, becoming part of the public electrical grid.</p>

      <h2>Why This Matters</h2>
      
      <p>In rural Costa Rica, electrical infrastructure expansion often lags behind community growth. By privately funding this project and donating it to the public utility, Mar Azul is accelerating infrastructure development that might otherwise take years to complete through normal government processes.</p>
      
      <blockquote>
        "We're not just building a community — we're building the infrastructure that makes communities possible. When we invest in roads, water, and electricity, everyone benefits, not just Mar Azul residents."
      </blockquote>

      <h2>A Pattern of Community Investment</h2>
      
      <p>The electrical infrastructure project continues Mar Azul's track record of community investment:</p>
      
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Water infrastructure</strong> — Donated well and water system to ASADA Santa Marta, serving 250+ families</li>
        <li><strong>Annual Christmas event</strong> — Five consecutive years providing gifts and celebration for 200+ local children</li>
        <li><strong>Road improvements</strong> — Ongoing investment in access roads that serve the entire area</li>
        <li><strong>Local employment</strong> — Prioritizing Nosara-area workers for construction and operations</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Working with ICE</h2>
      
      <p>The project is being developed in close coordination with ICE to ensure all infrastructure meets national standards and can be seamlessly integrated into the public grid. ICE engineers have been involved in the planning process, and the utility will take over maintenance and operation once the donation is complete.</p>

      <h2>About Mar Azul</h2>
      
      <p>Mar Azul is a private residential community in Nosara, Costa Rica, developed with the philosophy that private investment should benefit the broader community. Located in the Nicoya Peninsula Blue Zone, Mar Azul combines luxury living with genuine commitment to local infrastructure and community development.</p>
      
      <p><a href="/developments/mar-azul">Learn more about Mar Azul →</a></p>
    </div>

    <footer class="post-footer">
      <div class="tags">
        <span>Tags:</span>
        <a href="/blog/tag/infrastructure">Infrastructure</a>
        <a href="/blog/tag/community">Community</a>
        <a href="/blog/tag/mar-azul">Mar Azul</a>
        <a href="/blog/tag/nosara">Nosara</a>
        <a href="/blog/tag/ice">ICE</a>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .blog-post {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 4rem 2rem;
  }

  .post-header {
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .category {
    color: #3D4F3D;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 2px;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  h1 {
    font-family: Georgia, serif;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
    color: #1A1F16;
    line-height: 1.2;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .subtitle {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: #666;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  time {
    color: #888;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
  }

  .hero-image {
    margin: 2rem 0;
  }

  .hero-image img {
    width: 100%;
    border-radius: 8px;
  }

  .hero-image figcaption {
    text-align: center;
    color: #888;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }

  .post-content {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: #333;
  }

  .post-content h2 {
    font-family: Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 1.75rem;
    color: #1A1F16;
    margin: 2.5rem 0 1rem;
  }

  .post-content p {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .post-content ul {
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
  }

  .post-content li {
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .lead {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: #444;
    border-left: 4px solid #3D4F3D;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .stats-block {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 1.5rem;
    background: #F5F3EF;
    padding: 2rem;
    border-radius: 8px;
    margin: 2rem 0;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .stat .number {
    display: block;
    font-size: 2.5rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #3D4F3D;
  }

  .stat .label {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: #666;
  }

  blockquote {
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: #3D4F3D;
    border-left: 4px solid #C4A67C;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    margin: 2rem 0;
  }

  .post-footer {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding-top: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid #eee;
  }

  .tags {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .tags span {
    color: #888;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
  }

  .tags a {
    background: #F5F3EF;
    color: #3D4F3D;
    padding: 0.25rem 0.75rem;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .tags a:hover {
    background: #3D4F3D;
    color: white;
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .stats-block {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
